# Line-ending policy for this repo.
#
# `eol=lf` pins both the repo storage AND the working-tree extraction to LF on
# every platform. Modern Windows tooling (VS, VS Code, msbuild, dotnet CLI) all
# handle LF transparently, and matching working-tree to storage means the
# recurring "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it" warning
# never fires — it only appears when on-disk and repo line endings differ.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit text classifications so attribute decisions don't depend on heuristics
# for files added later.
*.cs        text diff=csharp
*.csproj    text
*.sln       text
*.slnx      text
*.props     text
*.targets   text
*.xaml      text
*.json      text
*.md        text
*.yml       text
*.yaml      text
*.sql       text
*.editorconfig text
.gitignore  text
.gitattributes text

# Explicit binaries — none in the repo today, but pin the rule for the common
# ones so future additions don't get accidentally line-ending-converted.
*.dll       binary
*.exe       binary
*.pdb       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.zip       binary
